course: dictionary
lesson: 12670
title: Distil
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Distil is a verb, so it is a doing word. It has a science meaning and a writing meaning. In science, to distil something means to heat a liquid until it turns to steam, then cool the steam back into liquid, so the liquid comes out pure. «The science teacher showed us how to distil salty water to get clean water.» Salt stays behind, and the clean water is collected.
explain: In writing, distil means to take the most important parts of a long text and put them into a short form. «Her summary managed to distil the whole story into three sentences.» She kept only the main points and left out the rest. Summarise is a close synonym here, but distil suggests that the words are boiled down, like a liquid made stronger and purer.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. Is there water, steam or a mixture nearby? Then it is probably the science meaning. Is there a long story, a book or main points? Then it is probably the writing meaning. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Distil means to make a liquid pure by heating it into steam and cooling the steam back into liquid.
fact: Distilled water is pure water, with the salt and other materials taken out. «Fill the iron with distilled water, not tap water.»
fact: Distil can also mean to make a strong drink like whisky in this way.
fact: «Distil the main points» means to shorten a text so only the most important ideas are left.
fact: Distil is related to the word distillation, which is the name for the process of distilling.
exercise: «The science teacher showed us how to distil salty water to get clean water.» What does distil mean here? | To add more salt to the water | To pour the water slowly into a bottle | *To make a liquid pure by heating it into steam and cooling it back | To freeze the water into solid ice
exercise: «Fill the iron with distilled water, not tap water.» What does distilled water mean? | Water that is frozen solid | Water that has been left out in the rain | Water with sugar mixed in | *Water made pure by heating it into steam and cooling it back
exercise: «Her summary managed to distil the whole story into three sentences.» What does distil mean here? | *To take the most important parts and put them in a short form | To make the story longer with more characters | To read the story out loud to a class | To draw a picture to go with the story
test: «The writer tried to distil the main points of the book into one page.» Which word is closest in meaning to distil here? | Forget | Expand | *Summarise | Decorate
test: What does distillation do in a science lesson? | It turns ice into a solid rock | *It separates pure liquid from a mixture, such as salty water | It mixes two liquids into a brand new colour | It makes a sound louder
exam: Ben says, «I will distil my notes into a few key points before the test.» What is Ben going to do? | Make his notes longer with more pictures | *Shorten his notes so only the key points are left | Throw his notes away and not revise | Copy his notes onto a new page in colour
